    {
      "id": "claim_ad1904edc67c4051b892fa0a6f216991",
      "statement": "The @tool decorator provides multiple usage patterns for creating tools from functions and Runnables: decorator without arguments (@tool), with custom name (@tool(\"name\")), with configuration parameters (@tool(...parameters...)), and wrapping Runnables (tool(\"name\", runnable)), automatically selecting between Tool and StructuredTool based on infer_schema configuration and handling schema inference from type hints and docstrings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/tools/convert.py#L77-L410",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1597ab6a8fd6aecf8b8fb03a2b1056c314ae0e5010a2340e1d85686b466c4527:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2510dcd5725047aa9d31804583d4dc73",
      "statement": "The @tool decorator accepts configuration parameters: description (with precedence: explicit > docstring > args_schema), return_direct (terminate agent loop), args_schema (explicit input schema), infer_schema (auto-generate schema from signature, default True), response_format (\"content\" or \"content_and_artifact\"), parse_docstring (extract descriptions from Google-style docstrings), error_on_invalid_docstring (raise on invalid docstring when parsing), and extras (provider-specific configuration like Anthropic cache_control).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/tools/convert.py#L77-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09dddb9b17b868996a4228e59b3dc28e64bda279cd195868f8ef7d81348cf9c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b078cac622354e6588c31a8ed9246b5d",
      "statement": "create_schema_from_function() generates a Pydantic model from function signatures by: extracting type hints including Annotated types, parsing Google-style docstrings if requested, merging descriptions from Annotated metadata and docstrings, filtering reserved parameters (run_manager, callbacks) and injected arguments, excluding synthetic Pydantic fields (args, kwargs) unless capturing *args/**kwargs, and excluding class/instance method self/cls parameters; supporting both Pydantic v1 and v2 annotations with error on mixed versions.",
